e-and-society","label":"Religions","content":"Anglican, Roman Catholic, Presbyterian, Baptist, Congregational, Methodist","ordinal":35,"locator":"factbook-2006/geos/gk.html#field:35","country":"GG","edition_year":2006},{"category":"people-and-society","label":"Languages","content":"English, French, Norman-French dialect spoken in country districts","ordinal":36,"locator":"factbook-2006/geos/gk.html#field:36","country":"GG","edition_year":2006},{"category":"people-and-society","label":"Literacy","content":"definition: NA\n\ntotal population: NA%\n\nmale: NA%\n\nfemale: NA%","ordinal":37,"locator":"factbook-2006/geos/gk.html#field:37","country":"GG","edition_year":2006},{"category":"government","label":"Country name","content":"conventional long form: Bailiwick of Guernsey\n\nconventional short form: Guernsey","ordinal":38,"locator":"factbook-2006/geos/gk.html#field:38","country":"GG","edition_year":2006},{"category":"government","label":"Dependency status","content":"British crown dependency","ordinal":39,"locator":"factbook-2006/geos/gk.html#field:39","country":"GG","edition_year":2006},{"category":"government","label":"Government type","content":"NA","ordinal":40,"locator":"factbook-2006/geos/gk.html#field:40","country":"GG","edition_year":2006},{"category":"government","label":"Capital","content":"name: Saint Peter Port\n\ngeographic coordinates: 49 27 N, 2 32 W\n\ntime difference: UTC 0 (5 hours ahead of Washington, DC during Standard Time)\n\ndaylight saving time: +1hr, begins last Sunday in March; ends last Sunday in October","ordinal":41,"locator":"factbook-2006/geos/gk.html#field:41","country":"GG","edition_year":2006},{"category":"government","label":"Administrative divisions","content":"none (British crown dependency); there are no first-order administrative divisions as defined by the US Government, but there are 10 parishes including Castel, Forest, Saint Andrew, Saint Martin, Saint Peter Port, Saint Pierre du Bois, Saint Sampson, Saint Saviour, Torteval, Vale","ordinal":42,"locator":"factbook-2006/geos/gk.html#field:42","country":"GG","edition_year":2006},{"category":"government","label":"Independence","content":"none (British crown dependency)","ordinal":43,"locator":"factbook-2006/geos/gk.html#field:43","country":"GG","edition_year":2006},{"category":"government","label":"National holiday","content":"Liberation Day, 9 May (1945)","ordinal":44,"locator":"factbook-2006/geos/gk.html#field:44","country":"GG","edition_year":2006},{"category":"government","label":"Constitution","content":"unwritten; partly statutes, partly common law and practice","ordinal":45,"locator":"factbook-2006/geos/gk.html#field:45","country":"GG","edition_year":2006},{"category":"government","label":"Legal system","content":"English law and local statutes; justice is administered by the Royal Court","ordinal":46,"locator":"factbook-2006/geos/gk.html#field:46","country":"GG","edition_year":2006},{"category":"government","label":"Suffrage","content":"18 years of age; universal","ordinal":47,"locator":"factbook-2006/geos/gk.html#field:47","country":"GG","edition_year":2006},{"category":"government","label":"Executive branch","content":"chief of state: Queen ELIZABETH II (since 6 February 1952), represented by Lieutenant Governor Sir Fabian MALBON (since 28 October 2005)\n\nhead of government: Chief Minister Laurie MORGAN (since 1 May 2004)\n\ncabinet: Policy Council elected by the States of Deliberation\n\nelections: the monarch is hereditary; lieutenant governor appointed by the monarch; chief minister is elected by States of Delibertion\n\nelection results: Laurie MORGAN elected chief minister, percent of vote of the States of Deliberation NA","ordinal":48,"locator":"factbook-2006/geos/gk.html#field:48","country":"GG","edition_year":2006},{"category":"government","label":"Legislative branch","content":"unicameral States of Deliberation (45 seats; members are elected by popular vote for four years); note - Alderney and Sark have their own parliaments\n\nelections: last held 21 April 2004 (next to be held in 2008)\n\nelection results: percent of vote - NA; seats - all independents","ordinal":49,"locator":"factbook-2006/geos/gk.html#field:49","country":"GG","edition_year":2006},{"category":"government","label":"Judicial branch","content":"Royal Court","ordinal":50,"locator":"factbook-2006/geos/gk.html#field:50","country":"GG","edition_year":2006},{"category":"government","label":"Political parties and leaders","content":"none; all independents","ordinal":51,"locator":"factbook-2006/geos/gk.html#field:51","country":"GG","edition_year":2006},{"category":"government","label":"Political pressure groups and leaders","content":"none","ordinal":52,"locator":"factbook-2006/geos/gk.html#field:52","country":"GG","edition_year":2006},{"category":"government","label":"International organization participation","content":"UPU","ordinal":53,"locator":"factbook-2006/geos/gk.html#field:53","country":"GG","edition_year":2006},{"category":"government","label":"Diplomatic representation in the US","content":"none (British crown dependency)","ordinal":54,"locator":"factbook-2006/geos/gk.html#field:54","country":"GG","edition_year":2006},{"category":"government","label":"Diplomatic representation from the US","content":"none (British crown dependency)","ordinal":55,"locator":"factbook-2006/geos/gk.html#field:55","country":"GG","edition_year":2006},{"category":"government","label":"Flag description","content":"white with the red cross of Saint George (patron saint of England) extending to the edges of the flag and a yellow equal-armed cross of William the Conqueror superimposed on the Saint George cross","ordinal":56,"locator":"factbook-2006/geos/gk.html#field:56","country":"GG","edition_year":2006},{"category":"economy","label":"Economy - overview","content":"Financial services - banking, fund management, insurance - account for about 55% of total income in this tiny, prosperous Channel Island economy. Tourism, manufacturing, and horticulture, mainly tomatoes and cut flowers, have been declining. Light tax and death duties make Guernsey a popular tax haven. The evolving economic integration of the EU nations is changing the environment under which Guernsey operates.","ordinal":57,"locator":"factbook-2006/geos/gk.html#field:57","country":"GG","edition_year":2006},{"category":"economy","label":"GDP (purchasing power parity)","content":"$2.59 billion (2003 est.)","ordinal":58,"locator":"factbook-2006/geos/gk.html#field:58","country":"GG","edition_year":2006},{"category":"economy","label":"GDP (official exchange rate)","content":"NA","ordinal":59,"locator":"factbook-2006/geos/gk.html#field:59","country":"GG","edition_year":2006},{"category":"economy","label":"GDP - real growth rate","content":"3% (2003 est.)","ordinal":60,"locator":"factbook-2006/geos/gk.html#field:60","country":"GG","edition_year":2006},{"category":"economy","label":"GDP - per capita (PPP)","content":"$40,000 (2003 est.)","ordinal":61,"locator":"factbook-2006/geos/gk.html#field:61","country":"GG","edition_year":2006},{"category":"economy","label":"GDP - composition by sector","content":"agriculture: 3%\n\nindustry: 10%\n\nservices: 87% (2000)","ordinal":62,"locator":"factbook-2006/geos/gk.html#field:62","country":"GG","edition_year":2006},{"category":"economy","label":"Labor force","content":"32,290 (2001)","ordinal":63,"locator":"factbook-2006/geos/gk.html#field:63","country":"GG","edition_year":2006},{"category":"economy","label":"Unemployment rate","content":"0.5% (1999 est.)","ordinal":64,"locator":"factbook-2006/geos/gk.html#field:64","country":"GG","edition_year":2006},{"category":"economy","label":"Population below poverty line","content":"NA%","ordinal":65,"locator":"factbook-2006/geos/gk.html#field:65","country":"GG","edition_year":2006},{"category":"economy","label":"Household income or consumption by percentage share","content":"lowest 10%: NA%\n\nhighest 10%: NA%","ordinal":66,"locator":"factbook-2006/geos/gk.html#